{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ccdf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0785b-9847-7fa3-b40c-313061570fc0"},"sequence":1226,"recorded_at":1780531400002447,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5f283545-6d77-4246-bbdf-5a980fc43a74","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5f283545-6d77-4246-bbdf-5a980fc43a74","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5f283545-6d77-4246-bbdf-5a980fc43a74"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"15ad15c4-858a-4436-aa07-64172b842a08"},"task_id":"15ad15c4-858a-4436-aa07-64172b842a08","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"15ad15c4-858a-4436-aa07-64172b842a08","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`.\n1|// AST-derived refusal-arm inventory for the terminal backend packages.\n2|//\n3|// The failure this file exists to prevent: a brand-new production refusal\n4|// arm carrying a brand-new unasserted detail shipped while `gofmt`,\n5|// `go vet`, `go test ./...`, and `tracecheck` all stayed green. A\n6|// hand-maintained arm list cannot catch that; a derived one can, but only\n7|// if it is checked in BOTH directions. The forward direction alone passes\n8|// vacuously on a truncated derivation: every derived arm asserted is true\n9|// when the derivation silently dropped half the package. So this file\n10|// derives every refusal arm from the production AST, requires each to\n11|// resolve to exactly one declared row naming a real asserting test, and\n12|// requires every declared row to resolve to exactly one derived arm.\n13|//\n14|// Modelled on internal/canonicaljson/grammar_inventory_test.go: derivation\n15|// fails closed on an empty, short, or unparseable input, and the declared\n16|// table cannot move its own goalposts because the derivation never\n17|// consults it.\n18|//\n19|// Stated bounds (not inferred):\n20|//   - The inventory proves every arm is DECLARED with a resolving test.\n21|//     Execution and decision proof is each row's named test, measured by\n22|//     this package's suite. A row resolves textually (detail mention, or\n23|//     entry-plus-code/predicate mention); a wrongly attributed row that\n24|//     still resolves is a review finding, not a green light.\n25|//   - Attribution drift survives through that fallback: a\n26|//     dead-by-construction arm can resolve through a sibling site's test\n27|//     while pointing at the wrong guard. Live example: CheckTransition's\n28|//     \"operation vocabulary\" arm (conformance.go) is unreachable —\n29|//     ParseOperation admits exactly the ten operations transitionTable\n30|//     covers, so lookupTransition never misses — yet the row carries no\n31|//     bound and resolves through TestParseOperationAdmitsOnlyTheTenClosedOperations,\n32|//     which drives ParseOperation's own arm sharing the detail. The five\n33|//     re-parse arms are the contrast: they declare boundDefensiveReparse\n34|//     and TestDefensiveBoundsAreExactlyThese pins the set.\n35|//   - Kill inflation: both inventory directions fail on ANY added or\n36|//     deleted production arm by construction, so an arm-deleting mutant\n37|//     elsewhere reads as killed by the inventory alone with no behavioral\n38|//     change. Mutation scores measured with this file present are NOT\n39|//     comparable to pre-inventory scores; review the failing-test list,\n40|//     not just the exit code.\n41|//   - errors.New/fmt.Errorf sites are not wire refusals and carry no arm.\n42|//     They live only in validatePlatforms (funneled into one *Error arm\n43|//     whose detail set is pinned exactly) and DigestFile (I/O errors that\n44|//     must never be *Error). Both properties are asserted below, in every\n45|//     FuncDecl body plus every package-level var initializer, and any\n46|//     reference to either constructor outside direct-call position\n47|//     (e.g. `newPlain := errors.New`) fails the suite, so an aliased\n48|//     construction cannot ship unattributed.\n49|//   - The DigestFile half of that allowlist is function-wide with no\n50|//     detail pin, unlike validatePlatforms' derived exact set: a new\n51|//     errors.New on any path inside DigestFile passes the gate (and the\n52|//     never-wire behavioral assertion, which only drives the current\n53|//     paths). Disclosed, not closed.\n54|//   - Custom error types outside the two recognised spellings (*Error,\n55|//     errors.New, fmt.Errorf) are outside both derivations: a bespoke\n56|//     error type smuggled as a refusal survives. Disclosed, not closed.\n57|//   - Constructor Details are single static literals by assertion: the\n58|//     derivation fatals on any mismatchf/integrityFailure call without\n59|//     exactly one string-literal argument, so format-verb interpolation\n60|//     cannot enter the table. Zero multi-argument sites today; go vet's\n61|//     printf analyzer independently refuses a non-constant format string.\n62|package terminalbackend\n63|\n64|import (\n65|\t\"errors\"\n66|\t\"go/ast\"\n67|\t\"go/parser\"\n68|\t\"go/token\"\n69|\t\"os\"\n70|\t\"path/filepath\"\n71|\t\"strconv\"\n72|\t\"strings\"\n73|\t\"testing\"\n74|)\n75|\n76|// refusalArm is one derived production refusal: a wire-code *Error\n77|// construction site keyed by file, enclosing function (receiver-qualified\n78|// for methods), code symbol, static detail, and occurrence index within\n79|// that key. The index keeps two identical arms in one function distinct:\n80|// adding a second arm with an already-declared key fails on the missing\n81|// #2 row instead of hiding behind #1.\n82|type refusalArm struct {\n83|\tfile       string\n84|\tfunction   string\n85|\tcode       string\n86|\tdetail     string\n87|\toccurrence int\n88|}\n89|\n90|// constructorFunctions build refusals instead of issuing them. Their own\n91|// *Error sites are the funnel, not arms.\n92|var constructorFunctions = map[string]bool{\n93|\t\"mismatchf\":        true,\n94|\t\"integrityFailure\": true,\n95|}\n96|\n97|// passthroughDetail marks the single dynamic-detail funnel: Registration\n98|// validation wraps validatePlatforms errors via err.Error(). Every other\n99|// Detail expression must be a static string literal; a new dynamic detail\n100|// fails the derivation rather than entering the table silently.\n101|const passthroughDetail = \"passthrough:err.Error()\"\n102|\n103|// deriveRefusalArms walks every production file of this package (every\n104|// *.go except *_test.go, so a new production file is scanned without\n105|// anyone remembering it) and returns every refusal arm in source order.\n106|// It fails closed: an unparseable file, a non-static code or detail, and\n107|// an empty result are all fatal, never an empty table.\n108|//\n109|// Coverage is declaration-complete, not FuncDecl-complete: every FuncDecl\n110|// body (including nested func literals, methods, and init) plus every\n111|// package-level var initializer is scanned, so a refusal arm hiding in a\n112|// package-level `var f = func() *Error {...}` is derived like any other.\n113|// Constructor references outside direct-call position (`refuse :=\n114|// mismatchf`) are rejected outright by rejectConstructorAliases below:\n115|// an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, so it fails the suite rather\n116|// than shipping silently.\n117|func deriveRefusalArms(t *testing.T) []refusalArm {\n118|\tt.Helper()\n119|\n120|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n121|\tif err != nil {\n122|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n123|\t}\n124|\tvar production []string\n125|\tfor _, match := range matches {\n126|\t\tif !strings.HasSuffix(match, \"_test.go\") {\n127|\t\t\tproduction = append(production, match)\n128|\t\t}\n129|\t}\n130|\tif len(production) == 0 {\n131|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n132|\t}\n133|\n134|\tvar arms []refusalArm\n135|\tparsed := 0\n136|\tfor _, name := range production {\n137|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n138|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n139|\t\tif err != nil {\n140|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v; an unparseable derivation proves nothing\", name, err)\n141|\t\t}\n142|\t\tparsed++\n143|\t\tcollect := func(functionName string, root ast.Node) {\n144|\t\t\tast.Inspect(root, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n145|\t\t\t\tswitch expression := node.(type) {\n146|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.UnaryExpr:\n147|\t\t\t\t\tif expression.Op != token.AND {\n148|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n149|\t\t\t\t\t}\n150|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := expression.X.(*ast.CompositeLit)\n151|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n152|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n153|\t\t\t\t\t}\n154|\t\t\t\t\tidentifier, ok := literal.Type.(*ast.Ident)\n155|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || identifier.Name != \"Error\" {\n156|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n157|\t\t\t\t\t}\n158|\t\t\t\t\tcode, detail := \"\", \"\"\n159|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, element := range literal.Elts {\n160|\t\t\t\t\t\tpair, ok := element.(*ast.KeyValueExpr)\n161|\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n162|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n163|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n164|\t\t\t\t\t\tkey, ok := pair.Key.(*ast.Ident)\n165|\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n166|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n167|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n168|\t\t\t\t\t\tswitch key.Name {\n169|\t\t\t\t\t\tcase \"Code\":\n170|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsymbol, ok := pair.Value.(*ast.Ident)\n171|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n172|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal code is not a static Code symbol; \"+\n173|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"a computed code cannot be inventoried\", functionName)\n174|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n175|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcode = symbol.Name\n176|\t\t\t\t\t\tcase \"Detail\":\n177|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdetail = staticDetail(t, functionName, pair.Value)\n178|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n179|\t\t\t\t\t}\n180|\t\t\t\t\tif code == \"\" || detail == \"\" {\n181|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal without a static code and detail; \"+\n182|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"the inventory cannot name what it cannot read\", functionName)\n183|\t\t\t\t\t}\n184|\t\t\t\t\tarms = append(arms, refusalArm{\n185|\t\t\t\t\t\tfile: name, function: functionName, code: code, detail: detail,\n186|\t\t\t\t\t})\n187|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.CallExpr:\n188|\t\t\t\t\tidentifier, ok := expression.Fun.(*ast.Ident)\n189|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || !constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] {\n190|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n191|\t\t\t\t\t}\n192|\t\t\t\t\tif len(expression.Args) != 1 {\n193|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: %s with %d arguments; Detail must be a single \"+\n194|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"static literal and never interpolate local data, and a \"+\n195|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"variadic detail cannot be inventoried\",\n196|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName, identifier.Name, len(expression.Args))\n197|\t\t\t\t\t}\n198|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := expression.Args[0].(*ast.BasicLit)\n199|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || literal.Kind != token.STRING {\n200|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: %s detail is not a static string literal; \"+\n201|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"a computed detail cannot be inventoried\", functionName, identifier.Name)\n202|\t\t\t\t\t}\n203|\t\t\t\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n204|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n205|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: unquote detail: %v\", functionName, err)\n206|\t\t\t\t\t}\n207|\t\t\t\t\tcode := \"CodeMismatch\"\n208|\t\t\t\t\tif identifier.Name == \"integrityFailure\" {\n209|\t\t\t\t\t\tcode = \"CodeIntegrityFailure\"\n210|\t\t\t\t\t}\n211|\t\t\t\t\tarms = append(arms, refusalArm{\n212|\t\t\t\t\t\tfile: name, function: functionName, code: code, detail: detail,\n213|\t\t\t\t\t})\n214|\t\t\t\t}\n215|\t\t\t\treturn true\n216|\t\t\t})\n217|\t\t}\n218|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n219|\t\t\tswitch decl := declaration.(type) {\n220|\t\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl:\n221|\t\t\t\tif decl.Body == nil {\n222|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n223|\t\t\t\t}\n224|\t\t\t\tif constructorFunctions[decl.Name.Name] {\n225|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n226|\t\t\t\t}\n227|\t\t\t\tfunctionName := decl.Name.Name\n228|\t\t\t\tif decl.Recv != nil && len(decl.Recv.List) > 0 {\n229|\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName = receiverTypeName(decl.Recv.List[0].Type) + \".\" + functionName\n230|\t\t\t\t}\n231|\t\t\t\tcollect(functionName, decl.Body)\n232|\t\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n233|\t\t\t\t// Package-level initializers execute outside any FuncDecl,\n234|\t\t\t\t// so a func literal (or a bare &Error{}) assigned to a\n235|\t\t\t\t// package var would otherwise ship invisible. Attribute\n236|\t\t\t\t// its arms to the declared variable name.\n237|\t\t\t\tfor _, spec := range decl.Specs {\n238|\t\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := spec.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n239|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n240|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n241|\t\t\t\t\t}\n242|\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName := \"var\"\n243|\t\t\t\t\tif len(value.Names) > 0 {\n244|\t\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName = value.Names[0].Name\n245|\t\t\t\t\t}\n246|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, item := range value.Values {\n247|\t\t\t\t\t\tcollect(functionName, item)\n248|\t\t\t\t\t}\n249|\t\t\t\t}\n250|\t\t\t}\n251|\t\t}\n252|\t\trejectConstructorAliases(t, file, name)\n253|\t}\n254|\t_ = parsed\n255|\tif len(arms) == 0 {\n256|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero refusal arms from the package sources; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n257|\t}\n258|\toccurrences := make(map[refusalArm]int)\n259|\tfor index := range arms {\n260|\t\tkey := arms[index]\n261|\t\tkey.occurrence = 0\n262|\t\toccurrences[key]++\n263|\t\tarms[index].occurrence = occurrences[key]\n264|\t}\n265|\treturn arms\n266|}\n267|\n268|// rejectConstructorAliases fails the suite when a refusal constructor\n269|// (mismatchf, integrityFailure) is referenced outside direct-call\n270|// position. `refuse := mismatchf; refuse(\"…\")` ships a reachable arm the\n271|// arm derivation above cannot attribute to a static call site, so the\n272|// reference itself is the violation: call the constructor directly.\n273|// The constructors' own declarations are excluded; their bodies are the\n274|// funnel, not arms. Any other use — alias, argument, field, shadow —\n275|// fails closed, because no legitimate production shape needs it.\n276|func rejectConstructorAliases(t *testing.T, file *ast.File, name string) {\n277|\tt.Helper()\n278|\n279|\tallowed := map[token.Pos]bool{}\n280|\tast.Inspect(file, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n281|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n282|\t\tif !ok {\n283|\t\t\tif call, ok := node.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n284|\t\t\t\tif identifier, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.Ident); ok && constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] {\n285|\t\t\t\t\tallowed[identifier.Pos()] = true\n286|\t\t\t\t}\n287|\t\t\t}\n288|\t\t\treturn true\n289|\t\t}\n290|\t\tif constructorFunctions[declaration.Name.Name] {\n291|\t\t\tallowed[declaration.Name.Pos()] = true\n292|\t\t\treturn false\n293|\t\t}\n294|\t\treturn true\n295|\t})\n296|\tast.Inspect(file, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n297|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n298|\t\tif ok && constructorFunctions[declaration.Name.Name] {\n299|\t\t\treturn false\n300|\t\t}\n301|\t\tidentifier, ok := node.(*ast.Ident)\n302|\t\tif !ok || !constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] || allowed[identifier.Pos()] {\n303|\t\t\treturn true\n304|\t\t}\n305|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: constructor %q referenced outside direct-call position; \"+\n306|\t\t\t\"an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, call it directly\", name, identifier.Name)\n307|\t\treturn true\n308|\t})\n309|}\n310|\n311|// receiverTypeName renders a method receiver type to its bare name.\n312|func receiverTypeName(expression ast.Expr) string {\n313|\tswitch typed := expression.(type) {\n314|\tcase *ast.Ident:\n315|\t\treturn typed.Name\n316|\tcase *ast.StarExpr:\n317|\t\treturn receiverTypeName(typed.X)\n318|\tdefault:\n319|\t\treturn \"unknown\"\n320|\t}\n321|}\n322|\n323|// staticDetail reads one Detail expression: a string literal, or the one\n324|// dynamic funnel. Anything else fails the derivation.\n325|func staticDetail(t *testing.T, function string, expression ast.Expr) string {\n326|\tt.Helper()\n327|\n328|\tif literal, ok := expression.(*ast.BasicLit); ok && literal.Kind == token.STRING {\n329|\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n330|\t\tif err != nil {\n331|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: unquote detail: %v\", function, err)\n332|\t\t}\n333|\t\treturn detail\n334|\t}\n335|\tif call, ok := expression.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n336|\t\tif selector, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.SelectorExpr); ok && selector.Sel.Name == \"Error\" {\n337|\t\t\tif receiver, ok := selector.X.(*ast.Ident); ok && receiver.Name == \"err\" {\n338|\t\t\t\treturn passthroughDetail\n339|\t\t\t}\n340|\t\t}\n341|\t}\n342|\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal Detail is not a static clause; Detail must never \"+\n343|\t\t\"interpolate local data, and a dynamic detail cannot be inventoried\", function)\n344|\treturn \"\"\n345|}\n346|\n347|// productionCodeSymbols resolves every Code symbol to its wire value from\n348|// the production const declarations, so the declared table cannot drift\n349|// from the codes production actually emits.\n350|func productionCodeSymbols(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n351|\tt.Helper()\n352|\n353|\tsymbols := make(map[string]string)\n354|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n355|\tif err != nil {\n356|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n357|\t}\n358|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n359|\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n360|\t\t\tcontinue\n361|\t\t}\n362|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n363|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n364|\t\tif err != nil {\n365|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n366|\t\t}\n367|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n368|\t\t\tgeneral, ok := declaration.(*ast.GenDecl)\n369|\t\t\tif !ok || general.Tok != token.CONST {\n370|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n371|\t\t\t}\n372|\t\t\tfor _, specification := range general.Specs {\n373|\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := specification.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n374|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n375|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n376|\t\t\t\t}\n377|\t\t\t\tfor index, name := range value.Names {\n378|\t\t\t\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(name.Name, \"Code\") || index >= len(value.Values) {\n379|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n380|\t\t\t\t\t}\n381|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := value.Values[index].(*ast.BasicLit)\n382|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || literal.Kind != token.STRING {\n383|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"code symbol %s is not a static string; \"+\n384|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"wire codes must be literals\", name.Name)\n385|\t\t\t\t\t}\n386|\t\t\t\t\twire, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n387|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n388|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unquote %s: %v\", name.Name, err)\n389|\t\t\t\t\t}\n390|\t\t\t\t\tsymbols[name.Name] = wire\n391|\t\t\t\t}\n392|\t\t\t}\n393|\t\t}\n394|\t}\n395|\tif len(symbols) == 0 {\n396|\t\tt.Fatal(\"resolved zero code symbols; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n397|\t}\n398|\treturn symbols\n399|}\n400|\n401|// testBodies indexes every test declaration in this package by file and\n402|// name to its body source. A duplicate test name across files fails: row\n403|// references would be ambiguous.\n404|func testBodies(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n405|\tt.Helper()\n406|\n407|\tbodies := make(map[string]string)\n408|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*_test.go\")\n409|\tif err != nil {\n410|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob test files: %v\", err)\n411|\t}\n412|\tif len(matches) == 0 {\n413|\t\tt.Fatal(\"found zero test files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n414|\t}\n415|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n416|\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(name)\n417|\t\tif err != nil {\n418|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read %s: %v\", name, err)\n419|\t\t}\n420|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n421|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n422|\t\tif err != nil {\n423|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n424|\t\t}\n425|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n426|\t\t\tfunction, ok := declaration.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n427|\t\t\tif !ok || !strings.HasPrefix(function.Name.Name, \"Test\") {\n428|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n429|\t\t\t}\n430|\t\t\tstart := fileSet.Position(function.Body.Pos()).Offset\n431|\t\t\tend := fileSet.Position(function.Body.End()).Offset\n432|\t\t\tkey := name + \"\\n\" + function.Name.Name\n433|\t\t\tif _, duplicate := bodies[key]; duplicate {\n434|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"test %s is declared twice; row references would be ambiguous\", key)\n435|\t\t\t}\n436|\t\t\tbodies[key] = string(raw[start:end])\n437|\t\t}\n438|\t}\n439|\tif len(bodies) == 0 {\n440|\t\tt.Fatal(\"indexed zero test declarations, so every row below would resolve vacuously\")\n441|\t}\n442|\treturn bodies\n443|}\n444|\n445|// predicateCodes resolves every Is predicate to the code symbol it\n446|// reports, verifying the shape: a single return of errorCode(err, Code).\n447|// A predicate in any other shape fails: the inventory leans on these to\n448|// resolve code-only assertions, so an unrecognized shape proves nothing.\n449|func predicateCodes(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n450|\tt.Helper()\n451|\n452|\tpredicates := make(map[string]string)\n453|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n454|\tif err != nil {\n455|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n456|\t}\n457|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n458|\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n459|\t\t\tcontinue\n460|\t\t}\n461|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n462|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n463|\t\tif err != nil {\n464|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n465|\t\t}\n466|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n467|\t\t\tfunction, ok := declaration.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n468|\t\t\tif !ok || !strings.HasPrefix(function.Name.Name, \"Is\") || function.Body == nil {\n469|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n470|\t\t\t}\n471|\t\t\tif len(function.Body.List) != 1 {\n472|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s is not a single return; the inventory cannot resolve it\",\n473|\t\t\t\t\tfunction.Name.Name)\n474|\t\t\t}\n475|\t\t\treturned, ok := function.Body.List[0].(*ast.ReturnStmt)\n476|\t\t\tif !ok || len(returned.Results) != 1 {\n477|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s is not a single return; the inventory cannot resolve it\",\n478|\t\t\t\t\tfunction.Name.Name)\n479|\t\t\t}\n480|\t\t\tcall, ok := returned.Results[0].(*ast.CallExpr)\n481|\t\t\tif !ok || len(call.Args) != 2 {\n482|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s does not call errorCode(err, Code); \"+\n483|\t\t\t\t\t\"the inventory cannot resolve it\", function.Name.Name)\n484|\t\t\t}\n485|\t\t\tcode, ok := call.Args[1].(*ast.Ident)\n486|\t\t\tif !ok {\n487|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s reports a non-static code; the inventory cannot resolve it\",\n488|\t\t\t\t\tfunction.Name.Name)\n489|\t\t\t}\n490|\t\t\tpredicates[function.Name.Name] = code.Name\n491|\t\t}\n492|\t}\n493|\tif len(predicates) == 0 {\n494|\t\tt.Fatal(\"resolved zero predicates; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n495|\t}\n496|\treturn predicates\n497|}\n498|\n499|// refusalTestRef names one asserting test by file and declaration name.\n500|type refusalTestRef struct {\n(more lines below)"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cce1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0785b-9847-7fa3-b40c-313061570fc0"},"sequence":1227,"recorded_at":1780531400002449,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5f283545-6d77-4246-bbdf-5a980fc43a74","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5f283545-6d77-4246-bbdf-5a980fc43a74","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5f283545-6d77-4246-bbdf-5a980fc43a74"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"15ad15c4-858a-4436-aa07-64172b842a08"},"task_id":"15ad15c4-858a-4436-aa07-64172b842a08","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"15ad15c4-858a-4436-aa07-64172b842a08"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cce3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0785b-9847-7fa3-b40c-313061570fc0"},"sequence":1228,"recorded_at":1780531400002451,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5f283545-6d77-4246-bbdf-5a980fc43a74","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"5f283545-6d77-4246-bbdf-5a980fc43a74","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5f283545-6d77-4246-bbdf-5a980fc43a74"},"call_id":"call_01a0786320747650bb2dec8599a53741","text":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`.\n1|// AST-derived refusal-arm inventory for the terminal backend packages.\n2|//\n3|// The failure this file exists to prevent: a brand-new production refusal\n4|// arm carrying a brand-new unasserted detail shipped while `gofmt`,\n5|// `go vet`, `go test ./...`, and `tracecheck` all stayed green. A\n6|// hand-maintained arm list cannot catch that; a derived one can, but only\n7|// if it is checked in BOTH directions. The forward direction alone passes\n8|// vacuously on a truncated derivation: every derived arm asserted is true\n9|// when the derivation silently dropped half the package. So this file\n10|// derives every refusal arm from the production AST, requires each to\n11|// resolve to exactly one declared row naming a real asserting test, and\n12|// requires every declared row to resolve to exactly one derived arm.\n13|//\n14|// Modelled on internal/canonicaljson/grammar_inventory_test.go: derivation\n15|// fails closed on an empty, short, or unparseable input, and the declared\n16|// table cannot move its own goalposts because the derivation never\n17|// consults it.\n18|//\n19|// Stated bounds (not inferred):\n20|//   - The inventory proves every arm is DECLARED with a resolving test.\n21|//     Execution and decision proof is each row's named test, measured by\n22|//     this package's suite. A row resolves textually (detail mention, or\n23|//     entry-plus-code/predicate mention); a wrongly attributed row that\n24|//     still resolves is a review finding, not a green light.\n25|//   - Attribution drift survives through that fallback: a\n26|//     dead-by-construction arm can resolve through a sibling site's test\n27|//     while pointing at the wrong guard. Live example: CheckTransition's\n28|//     \"operation vocabulary\" arm (conformance.go) is unreachable —\n29|//     ParseOperation admits exactly the ten operations transitionTable\n30|//     covers, so lookupTransition never misses — yet the row carries no\n31|//     bound and resolves through TestParseOperationAdmitsOnlyTheTenClosedOperations,\n32|//     which drives ParseOperation's own arm sharing the detail. The five\n33|//     re-parse arms are the contrast: they declare boundDefensiveReparse\n34|//     and TestDefensiveBoundsAreExactlyThese pins the set.\n35|//   - Kill inflation: both inventory directions fail on ANY added or\n36|//     deleted production arm by construction, so an arm-deleting mutant\n37|//     elsewhere reads as killed by the inventory alone with no behavioral\n38|//     change. Mutation scores measured with this file present are NOT\n39|//     comparable to pre-inventory scores; review the failing-test list,\n40|//     not just the exit code.\n41|//   - errors.New/fmt.Errorf sites are not wire refusals and carry no arm.\n42|//     They live only in validatePlatforms (funneled into one *Error arm\n43|//     whose detail set is pinned exactly) and DigestFile (I/O errors that\n44|//     must never be *Error). Both properties are asserted below, in every\n45|//     FuncDecl body plus every package-level var initializer, and any\n46|//     reference to either constructor outside direct-call position\n47|//     (e.g. `newPlain := errors.New`) fails the suite, so an aliased\n48|//     construction cannot ship unattributed.\n49|//   - The DigestFile half of that allowlist is function-wide with no\n50|//     detail pin, unlike validatePlatforms' derived exact set: a new\n51|//     errors.New on any path inside DigestFile passes the gate (and the\n52|//     never-wire behavioral assertion, which only drives the current\n53|//     paths). Disclosed, not closed.\n54|//   - Custom error types outside the two recognised spellings (*Error,\n55|//     errors.New, fmt.Errorf) are outside both derivations: a bespoke\n56|//     error type smuggled as a refusal survives. Disclosed, not closed.\n57|//   - Constructor Details are single static literals by assertion: the\n58|//     derivation fatals on any mismatchf/integrityFailure call without\n59|//     exactly one string-literal argument, so format-verb interpolation\n60|//     cannot enter the table. Zero multi-argument sites today; go vet's\n61|//     printf analyzer independently refuses a non-constant format string.\n62|package terminalbackend\n63|\n64|import (\n65|\t\"errors\"\n66|\t\"go/ast\"\n67|\t\"go/parser\"\n68|\t\"go/token\"\n69|\t\"os\"\n70|\t\"path/filepath\"\n71|\t\"strconv\"\n72|\t\"strings\"\n73|\t\"testing\"\n74|)\n75|\n76|// refusalArm is one derived production refusal: a wire-code *Error\n77|// construction site keyed by file, enclosing function (receiver-qualified\n78|// for methods), code symbol, static detail, and occurrence index within\n79|// that key. The index keeps two identical arms in one function distinct:\n80|// adding a second arm with an already-declared key fails on the missing\n81|// #2 row instead of hiding behind #1.\n82|type refusalArm struct {\n83|\tfile       string\n84|\tfunction   string\n85|\tcode       string\n86|\tdetail     string\n87|\toccurrence int\n88|}\n89|\n90|// constructorFunctions build refusals instead of issuing them. Their own\n91|// *Error sites are the funnel, not arms.\n92|var constructorFunctions = map[string]bool{\n93|\t\"mismatchf\":        true,\n94|\t\"integrityFailure\": true,\n95|}\n96|\n97|// passthroughDetail marks the single dynamic-detail funnel: Registration\n98|// validation wraps validatePlatforms errors via err.Error(). Every other\n99|// Detail expression must be a static string literal; a new dynamic detail\n100|// fails the derivation rather than entering the table silently.\n101|const passthroughDetail = \"passthrough:err.Error()\"\n102|\n103|// deriveRefusalArms walks every production file of this package (every\n104|// *.go except *_test.go, so a new production file is scanned without\n105|// anyone remembering it) and returns every refusal arm in source order.\n106|// It fails closed: an unparseable file, a non-static code or detail, and\n107|// an empty result are all fatal, never an empty table.\n108|//\n109|// Coverage is declaration-complete, not FuncDecl-complete: every FuncDecl\n110|// body (including nested func literals, methods, and init) plus every\n111|// package-level var initializer is scanned, so a refusal arm hiding in a\n112|// package-level `var f = func() *Error {...}` is derived like any other.\n113|// Constructor references outside direct-call position (`refuse :=\n114|// mismatchf`) are rejected outright by rejectConstructorAliases below:\n115|// an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, so it fails the suite rather\n116|// than shipping silently.\n117|func deriveRefusalArms(t *testing.T) []refusalArm {\n118|\tt.Helper()\n119|\n120|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n121|\tif err != nil {\n122|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n123|\t}\n124|\tvar production []string\n125|\tfor _, match := range matches {\n126|\t\tif !strings.HasSuffix(match, \"_test.go\") {\n127|\t\t\tproduction = append(production, match)\n128|\t\t}\n129|\t}\n130|\tif len(production) == 0 {\n131|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n132|\t}\n133|\n134|\tvar arms []refusalArm\n135|\tparsed := 0\n136|\tfor _, name := range production {\n137|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n138|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n139|\t\tif err != nil {\n140|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v; an unparseable derivation proves nothing\", name, err)\n141|\t\t}\n142|\t\tparsed++\n143|\t\tcollect := func(functionName string, root ast.Node) {\n144|\t\t\tast.Inspect(root, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n145|\t\t\t\tswitch expression := node.(type) {\n146|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.UnaryExpr:\n147|\t\t\t\t\tif expression.Op != token.AND {\n148|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n149|\t\t\t\t\t}\n150|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := expression.X.(*ast.CompositeLit)\n151|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n152|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n153|\t\t\t\t\t}\n154|\t\t\t\t\tidentifier, ok := literal.Type.(*ast.Ident)\n155|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || identifier.Name != \"Error\" {\n156|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n157|\t\t\t\t\t}\n158|\t\t\t\t\tcode, detail := \"\", \"\"\n159|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, element := range literal.Elts {\n160|\t\t\t\t\t\tpair, ok := element.(*ast.KeyValueExpr)\n161|\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n162|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n163|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n164|\t\t\t\t\t\tkey, ok := pair.Key.(*ast.Ident)\n165|\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n166|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n167|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n168|\t\t\t\t\t\tswitch key.Name {\n169|\t\t\t\t\t\tcase \"Code\":\n170|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsymbol, ok := pair.Value.(*ast.Ident)\n171|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n172|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal code is not a static Code symbol; \"+\n173|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"a computed code cannot be inventoried\", functionName)\n174|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n175|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcode = symbol.Name\n176|\t\t\t\t\t\tcase \"Detail\":\n177|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdetail = staticDetail(t, functionName, pair.Value)\n178|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n179|\t\t\t\t\t}\n180|\t\t\t\t\tif code == \"\" || detail == \"\" {\n181|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal without a static code and detail; \"+\n182|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"the inventory cannot name what it cannot read\", functionName)\n183|\t\t\t\t\t}\n184|\t\t\t\t\tarms = append(arms, refusalArm{\n185|\t\t\t\t\t\tfile: name, function: functionName, code: code, detail: detail,\n186|\t\t\t\t\t})\n187|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.CallExpr:\n188|\t\t\t\t\tidentifier, ok := expression.Fun.(*ast.Ident)\n189|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || !constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] {\n190|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n191|\t\t\t\t\t}\n192|\t\t\t\t\tif len(expression.Args) != 1 {\n193|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: %s with %d arguments; Detail must be a single \"+\n194|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"static literal and never interpolate local data, and a \"+\n195|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"variadic detail cannot be inventoried\",\n196|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName, identifier.Name, len(expression.Args))\n197|\t\t\t\t\t}\n198|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := expression.Args[0].(*ast.BasicLit)\n199|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || literal.Kind != token.STRING {\n200|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: %s detail is not a static string literal; \"+\n201|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"a computed detail cannot be inventoried\", functionName, identifier.Name)\n202|\t\t\t\t\t}\n203|\t\t\t\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n204|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n205|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: unquote detail: %v\", functionName, err)\n206|\t\t\t\t\t}\n207|\t\t\t\t\tcode := \"CodeMismatch\"\n208|\t\t\t\t\tif identifier.Name == \"integrityFailure\" {\n209|\t\t\t\t\t\tcode = \"CodeIntegrityFailure\"\n210|\t\t\t\t\t}\n211|\t\t\t\t\tarms = append(arms, refusalArm{\n212|\t\t\t\t\t\tfile: name, function: functionName, code: code, detail: detail,\n213|\t\t\t\t\t})\n214|\t\t\t\t}\n215|\t\t\t\treturn true\n216|\t\t\t})\n217|\t\t}\n218|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n219|\t\t\tswitch decl := declaration.(type) {\n220|\t\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl:\n221|\t\t\t\tif decl.Body == nil {\n222|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n223|\t\t\t\t}\n224|\t\t\t\tif constructorFunctions[decl.Name.Name] {\n225|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n226|\t\t\t\t}\n227|\t\t\t\tfunctionName := decl.Name.Name\n228|\t\t\t\tif decl.Recv != nil && len(decl.Recv.List) > 0 {\n229|\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName = receiverTypeName(decl.Recv.List[0].Type) + \".\" + functionName\n230|\t\t\t\t}\n231|\t\t\t\tcollect(functionName, decl.Body)\n232|\t\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n233|\t\t\t\t// Package-level initializers execute outside any FuncDecl,\n234|\t\t\t\t// so a func literal (or a bare &Error{}) assigned to a\n235|\t\t\t\t// package var would otherwise ship invisible. Attribute\n236|\t\t\t\t// its arms to the declared variable name.\n237|\t\t\t\tfor _, spec := range decl.Specs {\n238|\t\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := spec.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n239|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n240|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n241|\t\t\t\t\t}\n242|\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName := \"var\"\n243|\t\t\t\t\tif len(value.Names) > 0 {\n244|\t\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName = value.Names[0].Name\n245|\t\t\t\t\t}\n246|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, item := range value.Values {\n247|\t\t\t\t\t\tcollect(functionName, item)\n248|\t\t\t\t\t}\n249|\t\t\t\t}\n250|\t\t\t}\n251|\t\t}\n252|\t\trejectConstructorAliases(t, file, name)\n253|\t}\n254|\t_ = parsed\n255|\tif len(arms) == 0 {\n256|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero refusal arms from the package sources; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n257|\t}\n258|\toccurrences := make(map[refusalArm]int)\n259|\tfor index := range arms {\n260|\t\tkey := arms[index]\n261|\t\tkey.occurrence = 0\n262|\t\toccurrences[key]++\n263|\t\tarms[index].occurrence = occurrences[key]\n264|\t}\n265|\treturn arms\n266|}\n267|\n268|// rejectConstructorAliases fails the suite when a refusal constructor\n269|// (mismatchf, integrityFailure) is referenced outside direct-call\n270|// position. `refuse := mismatchf; refuse(\"…\")` ships a reachable arm the\n271|// arm derivation above cannot attribute to a static call site, so the\n272|// reference itself is the violation: call the constructor directly.\n273|// The constructors' own declarations are excluded; their bodies are the\n274|// funnel, not arms. Any other use — alias, argument, field, shadow —\n275|// fails closed, because no legitimate production shape needs it.\n276|func rejectConstructorAliases(t *testing.T, file *ast.File, name string) {\n277|\tt.Helper()\n278|\n279|\tallowed := map[token.Pos]bool{}\n280|\tast.Inspect(file, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n281|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n282|\t\tif !ok {\n283|\t\t\tif call, ok := node.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n284|\t\t\t\tif identifier, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.Ident); ok && constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] {\n285|\t\t\t\t\tallowed[identifier.Pos()] = true\n286|\t\t\t\t}\n287|\t\t\t}\n288|\t\t\treturn true\n289|\t\t}\n290|\t\tif constructorFunctions[declaration.Name.Name] {\n291|\t\t\tallowed[declaration.Name.Pos()] = true\n292|\t\t\treturn false\n293|\t\t}\n294|\t\treturn true\n295|\t})\n296|\tast.Inspect(file, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n297|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n298|\t\tif ok && constructorFunctions[declaration.Name.Name] {\n299|\t\t\treturn false\n300|\t\t}\n301|\t\tidentifier, ok := node.(*ast.Ident)\n302|\t\tif !ok || !constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] || allowed[identifier.Pos()] {\n303|\t\t\treturn true\n304|\t\t}\n305|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: constructor %q referenced outside direct-call position; \"+\n306|\t\t\t\"an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, call it directly\", name, identifier.Name)\n307|\t\treturn true\n308|\t})\n309|}\n310|\n311|// receiverTypeName renders a method receiver type to its bare name.\n312|func receiverTypeName(expression ast.Expr) string {\n313|\tswitch typed := expression.(type) {\n314|\tcase *ast.Ident:\n315|\t\treturn typed.Name\n316|\tcase *ast.StarExpr:\n317|\t\treturn receiverTypeName(typed.X)\n318|\tdefault:\n319|\t\treturn \"unknown\"\n320|\t}\n321|}\n322|\n323|// staticDetail reads one Detail expression: a string literal, or the one\n324|// dynamic funnel. Anything else fails the derivation.\n325|func staticDetail(t *testing.T, function string, expression ast.Expr) string {\n326|\tt.Helper()\n327|\n328|\tif literal, ok := expression.(*ast.BasicLit); ok && literal.Kind == token.STRING {\n329|\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n330|\t\tif err != nil {\n331|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: unquote detail: %v\", function, err)\n332|\t\t}\n333|\t\treturn detail\n334|\t}\n335|\tif call, ok := expression.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n336|\t\tif selector, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.SelectorExpr); ok && selector.Sel.Name == \"Error\" {\n337|\t\t\tif receiver, ok := selector.X.(*ast.Ident); ok && receiver.Name == \"err\" {\n338|\t\t\t\treturn passthroughDetail\n339|\t\t\t}\n340|\t\t}\n341|\t}\n342|\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal Detail is not a static clause; Detail must never \"+\n343|\t\t\"interpolate local data, and a dynamic detail cannot be inventoried\", function)\n344|\treturn \"\"\n345|}\n346|\n347|// productionCodeSymbols resolves every Code symbol to its wire value from\n348|// the production const declarations, so the declared table cannot drift\n349|// from the codes production actually emits.\n350|func productionCodeSymbols(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n351|\tt.Helper()\n352|\n353|\tsymbols := make(map[string]string)\n354|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n355|\tif err != nil {\n356|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n357|\t}\n358|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n359|\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n360|\t\t\tcontinue\n361|\t\t}\n362|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n363|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n364|\t\tif err != nil {\n365|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n366|\t\t}\n367|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n368|\t\t\tgeneral, ok := declaration.(*ast.GenDecl)\n369|\t\t\tif !ok || general.Tok != token.CONST {\n370|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n371|\t\t\t}\n372|\t\t\tfor _, specification := range general.Specs {\n373|\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := specification.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n374|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n375|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n376|\t\t\t\t}\n377|\t\t\t\tfor index, name := range value.Names {\n378|\t\t\t\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(name.Name, \"Code\") || index >= len(value.Values) {\n379|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n380|\t\t\t\t\t}\n381|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := value.Values[index].(*ast.BasicLit)\n382|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || literal.Kind != token.STRING {\n383|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"code symbol %s is not a static string; \"+\n384|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"wire codes must be literals\", name.Name)\n385|\t\t\t\t\t}\n386|\t\t\t\t\twire, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n387|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n388|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unquote %s: %v\", name.Name, err)\n389|\t\t\t\t\t}\n390|\t\t\t\t\tsymbols[name.Name] = wire\n391|\t\t\t\t}\n392|\t\t\t}\n393|\t\t}\n394|\t}\n395|\tif len(symbols) == 0 {\n396|\t\tt.Fatal(\"resolved zero code symbols; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n397|\t}\n398|\treturn symbols\n399|}\n400|\n401|// testBodies indexes every test declaration in this package by file and\n402|// name to its body source. A duplicate test name across files fails: row\n403|// references would be ambiguous.\n404|func testBodies(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n405|\tt.Helper()\n406|\n407|\tbodies := make(map[string]string)\n408|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*_test.go\")\n409|\tif err != nil {\n410|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob test files: %v\", err)\n411|\t}\n412|\tif len(matches) == 0 {\n413|\t\tt.Fatal(\"found zero test files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n414|\t}\n415|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n416|\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(name)\n417|\t\tif err != nil {\n418|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read %s: %v\", name, err)\n419|\t\t}\n420|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n421|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n422|\t\tif err != nil {\n423|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n424|\t\t}\n425|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n426|\t\t\tfunction, ok := declaration.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n427|\t\t\tif !ok || !strings.HasPrefix(function.Name.Name, \"Test\") {\n428|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n429|\t\t\t}\n430|\t\t\tstart := fileSet.Position(function.Body.Pos()).Offset\n431|\t\t\tend := fileSet.Position(function.Body.End()).Offset\n432|\t\t\tkey := name + \"\\n\" + function.Name.Name\n433|\t\t\tif _, duplicate := bodies[key]; duplicate {\n434|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"test %s is declared twice; row references would be ambiguous\", key)\n435|\t\t\t}\n436|\t\t\tbodies[key] = string(raw[start:end])\n437|\t\t}\n438|\t}\n439|\tif len(bodies) == 0 {\n440|\t\tt.Fatal(\"indexed zero test declarations, so every row below would resolve vacuously\")\n441|\t}\n442|\treturn bodies\n443|}\n444|\n445|// predicateCodes resolves every Is predicate to the code symbol it\n446|// reports, verifying the shape: a single return of errorCode(err, Code).\n447|// A predicate in any other shape fails: the inventory leans on these to\n448|// resolve code-only assertions, so an unrecognized shape proves nothing.\n449|func predicateCodes(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n450|\tt.Helper()\n451|\n452|\tpredicates := make(map[string]string)\n453|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n454|\tif err != nil {\n455|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n456|\t}\n457|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n458|\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n459|\t\t\tcontinue\n460|\t\t}\n461|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n462|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n463|\t\tif err != nil {\n464|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n465|\t\t}\n466|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n467|\t\t\tfunction, ok := declaration.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n468|\t\t\tif !ok || !strings.HasPrefix(function.Name.Name, \"Is\") || function.Body == nil {\n469|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n470|\t\t\t}\n471|\t\t\tif len(function.Body.List) != 1 {\n472|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s is not a single return; the inventory cannot resolve it\",\n473|\t\t\t\t\tfunction.Name.Name)\n474|\t\t\t}\n475|\t\t\treturned, ok := function.Body.List[0].(*ast.ReturnStmt)\n476|\t\t\tif !ok || len(returned.Results) != 1 {\n477|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s is not a single return; the inventory cannot resolve it\",\n478|\t\t\t\t\tfunction.Name.Name)\n479|\t\t\t}\n480|\t\t\tcall, ok := returned.Results[0].(*ast.CallExpr)\n481|\t\t\tif !ok || len(call.Args) != 2 {\n482|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s does not call errorCode(err, Code); \"+\n483|\t\t\t\t\t\"the inventory cannot resolve it\", function.Name.Name)\n484|\t\t\t}\n485|\t\t\tcode, ok := call.Args[1].(*ast.Ident)\n486|\t\t\tif !ok {\n487|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s reports a non-static code; the inventory cannot resolve it\",\n488|\t\t\t\t\tfunction.Name.Name)\n489|\t\t\t}\n490|\t\t\tpredicates[function.Name.Name] = code.Name\n491|\t\t}\n492|\t}\n493|\tif len(predicates) == 0 {\n494|\t\tt.Fatal(\"resolved zero predicates; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n495|\t}\n496|\treturn predicates\n497|}\n498|\n499|// refusalTestRef names one asserting test by file and declaration name.\n500|type refusalTestRef struct {\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
