{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cd07","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0785b-9847-7fa3-b40c-313061570fc0"},"sequence":1246,"recorded_at":1780531400002487,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5f283545-6d77-4246-bbdf-5a980fc43a74","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"5f283545-6d77-4246-bbdf-5a980fc43a74","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5f283545-6d77-4246-bbdf-5a980fc43a74"},"call_id":"call_01a078632d1870828d1c9af5901b7386","text":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`.\n(499 line(s) above)\n500|type refusalTestRef struct {\n501|\tfile string\n502|\ttest string\n503|}\n504|\n505|// declaredRefusalArm is one inventoried arm: the derived key (file,\n506|// function, code symbol, static detail, occurrence), the public\n507|// production entry its test drives, an optional stated bound for\n508|// defensive arms no document can reach, and the tests asserting it.\n509|type declaredRefusalArm struct {\n510|\tfile       string\n511|\tfunction   string\n512|\tcode       string\n513|\tdetail     string\n514|\toccurrence int\n515|\tentry      string\n516|\tbound      string\n517|\t// detailSet carries the funneled detail set for the single\n518|\t// dynamic-detail row; it is empty for every literal row.\n519|\tdetailSet []string\n520|\ttests     []refusalTestRef\n521|}\n522|\n523|// boundDefensiveReparse is the stated bound for re-parse arms after an\n524|// already-validated member: timestampMember validated the member, and the\n525|// Time re-parse cannot fail while scalar owns that contract. The arms\n526|// stay as fail-closed defense; the bound says why no document reaches\n527|// them, and TestDefensiveBoundsAreExactlyThese pins the set.\n528|const boundDefensiveReparse = \"defensive re-parse after validation; scalar owns the re-parse contract\"\n529|\n530|// declaredRefusalArms is the inventoried arm set. Field order is file,\n531|// function (receiver-qualified for methods), code symbol, static detail,\n532|// occurrence within that key, driven public entry, stated bound (empty\n533|// except for defensive arms), funneled detail set (nil except the funnel\n534|// row, which lives outside this table), and asserting tests.\n535|//\n536|// The table is generated from the derivation, never hand-enumerated:\n537|// every row must match exactly one derived arm and vice versa, so adding\n538|// a production arm without a row fails forward, and deleting one fails\n539|// in reverse.\n540|var declaredRefusalArms = []declaredRefusalArm{\n541|\t{\"conformance.go\", \"CheckAttachRequest\", \"CodeMismatch\", \"document timestamp\", 1, \"CheckAttachRequest\", boundDefensiveReparse, nil, []refusalTestRef{{file: \"conformance_test.go\", test: \"TestCheckAttachRequestBindsTransportInputAndExpiry\"}}},\n542|\t{\"conformance.go\", \"CheckAttachRequest\", \"CodeUnauthorized\", \"attach authorization binding\", 1, \"CheckAttachRequest\", \"\", nil, []refusalTestRef{{file: \"conformance_test.go\", test: \"TestCheckAttachRequestBindsTransportInputAndExpiry\"}}},\n543|\t{\"conformance.go\", \"CheckAttachRequest\", \"CodeUnauthorized\", \"attach authorization expiry\", 1, \"CheckAttachRequest\", \"\", nil, []refusalTestRef{{file: \"conformance_test.go\", test: \"TestCheckAttachRequestBindsTransportInputAndExpiry\"}}},\n544|\t{\"conformance.go\", \"CheckAttachRequest\", \"CodeUnauthorized\", \"attach relay transport\", 1, \"CheckAttachRequest\", \"\", nil, []refusalTestRef{{file: \"conformance_test.go\", test: \"TestCheckAttachRequestBindsTransportInputAndExpiry\"}}},\n545|\t{\"conformance.go\", \"CheckAttachResult\", \"CodeUnauthorized\", \"attach input binding\", 1, \"CheckAttachResult\", \"\", nil, []refusalTestRef{{file: \"conformance_test.go\", test: \"TestCheckAttachResultRequiresTripleEquality\"}}},\n546|\t{\"conformance.go\", \"CheckEntrypoint\", \"CodePreconditionFailed\", \"entrypoint argv\", 1, \"